# NestJS Code Review Checklist

Use when reviewing `backend/` changes. Report findings by severity: **blocker** / **warning** / **nit**.

## Architecture & contracts

- [ ] Matches `docs/db-schema.md`, `docs/api-doc.md`, architecture decisions
- [ ] API doc updated if endpoints or responses changed
- [ ] Module boundaries respected (entity / service / controller / DTO separate)

## Correctness

- [ ] Date validation: `expiryDate` > `issuedDate`
- [ ] Status computed server-side (Asia/Colombo + buffer); not client-writable
- [ ] Renewal creates new record; old → `renewed` (not `archived`)
- [ ] Employee archive cascades in single transaction
- [ ] `bulk-status` idempotent; skips renewed/archived/missing
- [ ] Soft-deleted records excluded from default lists and dashboard

## Security

- [ ] JwtAuthGuard on protected routes
- [ ] DTO validation on all inputs; enums enforced
- [ ] No secrets, raw SQL interpolation, or hard delete endpoints
- [ ] bcrypt for passwords; passwordHash never exposed

## Performance

- [ ] Pagination enforced (max 200); no N+1 queries
- [ ] Indexes considered for new filter/sort columns
- [ ] Dashboard uses live aggregation (no shadow summary table)

## Tests

- [ ] Unit/e2e tests for new behavior; regression test for bug fixes

## Output format

List each issue with file path, what's wrong, and suggested fix. If clean, state "no blockers found."
